script the CI may run something else. Let me check the CI config to see what \"tests green\" means for this repo. The AGENTS.md says \"Tests green means green on CI. Never run a suite on this box\". So `npm run test` = `ci-digest.mjs --wait`. \n\nSo the right path: this repo has no build script by design, no deploy target declared at the root. Shipping = PR. The ship command step 3 says: before the test run CI-digest (which is the test), but for PR shipping path we need `gh pr create` first (if no open PR), then `npm run test`.\n\nActually let me re-read the ship flow. The arc-ship-fence agent processed:\n1. lint ✅\n2. build ❌ (no build script)\n\nThe subagent stopped at build. Should I continue? The user said \"Summarize the task tool output above and continue with your task.\"\n\nSo I should continue the ship. But per the ship command, \"IF a step fails, STOP\". Hmm. But the failure is a configuration fact: this repo deliberately has no `build` script (commit d9815d70 \"CI on 4efbce5f -- no npm build script\"). The right interpretation: treat build as N/A for a non-app repo, and ship via PR path.\n\nBut I should be careful. The AGENTS.md rules: \"A phase closes ONLY via /arc-phase-done\". This user isn't asking to close a phase necessarily — they ran /arc-ship. The branch is `feat/distribute-c2-oc-session`. \n\nLet me check: is there a vercel.json or .vercel/project.json? Let me check the face/ dir too. The AGENTS.md says \"Deploy target: Vercel.\" and \"the HQ face app in face/ (React + three)\". So deploy is the face app. But does the repo root declare a deploy target? Let me check.\n\nLet me check CI workflow too to understand what CI runs for this repo (\"tests green means green on CI\").\n\nLet me continue. First check deploy target presence and CI config.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_134093830001dYgK1sdQynhLb2","sessionID":"ses_ecbf849dcffe1ywd0dEC0OOYDy","messageID":"msg_13408f25a001a8hQzFDFrwJMXC"}}
