o. CI runs bats self-tests, product-lint, version gate, etc. There's no `build` in CI either. So `npm run build` is genuinely N/A for this repo. The ship path is PR-based: create a PR, wait for CI, and report.\n\nThe ship command says:\n1. lint ✅ (done, green)\n2. build ❌ (no build script — N/A for this repo, CI doesn't build either)\n3. Ship path: branch has upstream `origin/feat/distribute-c2-oc-session`, no open PR. So create PR with `gh pr create --fill`, then `npm run test` (ci-digest wait).\n\nWait — the ship command says \"**the pre-deploy-guard hook will re-check tests**\" but no deploy target, so deploy: none declared — the PR is the ship. But the test step... Let me re-read.\n\nStep 3: \"before the test: run git branch --show-current and git rev-parse --abbrev-ref @{u}. If the branch has no upstream, or its upstream is not origin/<that branch>, STOP... Then run gh pr view ... and only if it finds no open PR for this branch, run gh pr create --fill. Then npm run test. When it exits 3 (CI still running: each call waits at most 9 minutes), run it again, up to 4 times in all; any other non-zero exit is a failure.\"\n\nStep 4: \"Deploy only if the repo declares a deploy target (vercel.json or .vercel/project.json exists) ... Otherwise do not deploy: print deploy: none declared — the PR is the ship, and use the PR's URL from gh pr view --json url,state as the URL below.\"\n\nSo the correct continuation is:\n1. build skipped because the repo has no build script and CI doesn't run npm build either (that's genuine N/A, not a failure — a harness repo whose \"build\" is its self-tests).\n2. Create the PR (none exists yet).\n3. Run `npm run test` (ci-digest wait).\n4. No deploy target → PR is the ship.\n\nBut wait — the AGENTS.md says \"Tests green means green on CI. Never run a suite on this box\". `npm run test` runs ci-digest, which reads CI — that matches the rule. Good.\n\nAlso need to consider: the `.opencode/` directory is untracked! `git status --short` showed `?? .opencode/`. That's concerning for the PR — the PR would include only committed changes. Let me check what the current uncommitted state is. `git status` showed only `?? .opencode/` as untracked. That's untracked so won't be in commits. But the PR diff is based on committed change vs main. Is there anything uncommitted that should be committed first? Let me check git status more carefully. The subagent said branch is `feat/distribute-c2-oc-session`. git log shows it's a merged tree with docs archive etc. \n\nActually, wait — this arc-ship was invoked with the intent to ship the current branch. Let me check what changed vs main to write a good summary. Actually `gh pr create --fill` fills from the branch name and commits. Let me check git status and how many commits the branch is ahead of main.\n\nLet me also verify the `.opencode/` untracked dir — it may contain session state that shouldn't be committed. The repo has `.gitignore`. Let me not commit anything myself; `gh pr create --fill` only uses committed state.\n\nLet me proceed: check git status/diff scope, then create the PR, then run the test watch.\n\nActually, one more consideration per the ship command: \"Run this branch check...\" — branches balance. The branch `feat/distribute-c2-oc-session` is genuinely current. Good.\n\nLet me check what the branch contains vs main for the summary.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_13409b58f001UT2lEvFbqeedcr","sessionID":"ses_ecbf849dcffe1ywd0dEC0OOYDy","messageID":"msg_1340971db001lSH33OQc4qEHCt"}}
