{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791874604020,"sessionID":"ses_ecbf849dcffe1ywd0dEC0OOYDy","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_8496619df1594accba0d225c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"E:\\Work_Hub\\01_Automemory\\wt-oc-req03\\docs\\runbooks\\distribute.md","offset":1,"limit":60},"output":"<path>E:\\Work_Hub\\01_Automemory\\wt-oc-req03\\docs\\runbooks\\distribute.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Runbook — `distribute`, arc in any harness\n2: \n3: arc is written once, in the Claude Code dialect under `.claude/`, and rendered for every other harness\n4: (ADR-2001). This runbook covers installing it, reading an install back, and changing what the render does.\n5: Decisions: ADR-2000–2018. The capability matrix is `engine/harnesses.yaml`, and the fate of each\n6: frontmatter key is `engine/frontmatter-keys.yaml`.\n7: \n8: ## Install arc into a project\n9: \n10: From a checkout of arc:\n11: \n12: ```bash\n13: node bin/arc.mjs init --target <claude-code|codex|opencode|skills-only> --dir /path/to/project [--dry-run] [--force]\n14: ```\n15: \n16: Or without a checkout. The package is never published (ADR-2008), so it installs from git or from a\n17: tarball:\n18: \n19: ```bash\n20: npm i -g github:technology-ashiq/arc#<commit> && arc init --target opencode --dir .\n21: npm pack /path/to/arc && npm i -g ./arc-*.tgz && arc init --target codex --dir .\n22: ```\n23: \n24: `sync-to-project.sh <dir>` is the same claude-code install with `--force`, plus the council `.env.example`\n25: block. `--products` mode is unchanged.\n26: \n27: | Target | What lands | What it cannot hold |\n28: |---|---|---|\n29: | `claude-code` | `.claude/` (minus local state), the meta docs, `CONSTITUTION.md`, the council skeleton | nothing: it is the source |\n30: | `codex` | the support payload, commands as `.agents/skills/NAME/SKILL.md` (invoked `$NAME`), agents as `.codex/agents/NAME.toml` | tool fences, argument hints, model tiers, `$ARGUMENTS` |\n31: | `opencode` | the support payload, `.opencode/commands/`, `.opencode/agents/` (each fenced command runs as a hidden `NAME-fence` subagent), `.opencode/skills/` | argument hints, model tiers; `arc-toolcheck` (needs `Artifact`) |\n32: | `skills-only` | the support payload and every command and agent as an agentskills.io skill under `.agents/skills/` | hooks, user-only invocation, `$ARGUMENTS`, hints, tiers |\n33: \n34: The **support payload** is the claude-code install minus what only Claude Code reads (`.claude/commands/`,\n35: `agents/`, `hooks/`, `output-styles/`, `skills/`, `settings.json`). The rendered commands still call\n36: `.claude/scripts/` and read `.claude/rules/`, so the payload ships with every target.\n37: \n38: `--dry-run` prints the plan, one `degraded:` line per `false` matrix cell and one `partial:` line per\n39: `partial:` cell, and writes nothing. A Claude-only command (`targets: claude-code`) is `[skipped]` on the\n40: other targets, and a construct a target cannot hold is `[unsupported]` by name, never paraphrased.\n41: \n42: In a git repo whose `core.hooksPath` is unset, `arc init` points it at `.claude/templates/githooks/`\n43: (branch guard and staged-secret scan). It leaves a project's own hooks path alone and says so.\n44: \n45: ## Read an install back\n46: \n47: ```bash\n48: node bin/arc.mjs doctor --dir /path/to/project     # or: node .claude/scripts/engine/arc-install.mjs --doctor DIR\n49: node bin/arc.mjs doctor                            # checks this copy of arc can install at all\n50: ```\n51: \n52: One line per managed path, then the counts:\n53: \n54: | State | Meaning | What to do |\n55: |---|---|---|\n56: | `placed` | on disk, byte-identical (CR bytes ignored) to what the install wrote | nothing |\n57: | `missing` | the install wrote it, and it is gone | re-run `arc init` with the same target |\n58: | `unmanaged-conflict` | something else is there: a hand edit, a link, a directory | keep it, or re-run with `--force`; the original goes to `.arc-install-backup/<stamp>/` |\n59: | `degraded` | a matrix cell the target cannot hold | nothing: it is a declared limit |\n60: \n\n(Showing lines 1-60 of 101. Use offset=61 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Runbook — `distribute`, arc in any harness\n\narc is written once, in the Claude Code dialect under `.claude/`, and rendered for every other harness\n(ADR-2001). This runbook covers installing it, reading an install back, and changing what the render does.\nDecisions: ADR-2000–2018. The capability matrix is `engine/harnesses.yaml`, and the fate of each\nfrontmatter key is `engine/frontmatter-keys.yaml`.\n\n## Install arc into a project\n\nFrom a checkout of arc:\n\n```bash\nnode bin/arc.mjs init --target <claude-code|codex|opencode|skills-only> --dir /path/to/project [--dry-run] [--force]\n```\n\nOr without a checkout. The package is never published (ADR-2008), so it installs from git or from a\ntarball:\n\n```bash\nnpm i -g github:technology-ashiq/arc#<commit> && arc init --target opencode --dir .","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"E:\\Work_Hub\\01_Automemory\\wt-oc-req03\\docs\\runbooks\\distribute.md","text":"# Runbook — `distribute`, arc in any harness\n\narc is written once, in the Claude Code dialect under `.claude/`, and rendered for every other harness\n(ADR-2001). This runbook covers installing it, reading an install back, and changing what the render does.\nDecisions: ADR-2000–2018. The capability matrix is `engine/harnesses.yaml`, and the fate of each\nfrontmatter key is `engine/frontmatter-keys.yaml`.\n\n## Install arc into a project\n\nFrom a checkout of arc:\n\n```bash\nnode bin/arc.mjs init --target <claude-code|codex|opencode|skills-only> --dir /path/to/project [--dry-run] [--force]\n```\n\nOr without a checkout. The package is never published (ADR-2008), so it installs from git or from a\ntarball:\n\n```bash\nnpm i -g github:technology-ashiq/arc#<commit> && arc init --target opencode --dir .\nnpm pack /path/to/arc && npm i -g ./arc-*.tgz && arc init --target codex --dir .\n```\n\n`sync-to-project.sh <dir>` is the same claude-code install with `--force`, plus the council `.env.example`\nblock. `--products` mode is unchanged.\n\n| Target | What lands | What it cannot hold |\n|---|---|---|\n| `claude-code` | `.claude/` (minus local state), the meta docs, `CONSTITUTION.md`, the council skeleton | nothing: it is the source |\n| `codex` | the support payload, commands as `.agents/skills/NAME/SKILL.md` (invoked `$NAME`), agents as `.codex/agents/NAME.toml` | tool fences, argument hints, model tiers, `$ARGUMENTS` |\n| `opencode` | the support payload, `.opencode/commands/`, `.opencode/agents/` (each fenced command runs as a hidden `NAME-fence` subagent), `.opencode/skills/` | argument hints, model tiers; `arc-toolcheck` (needs `Artifact`) |\n| `skills-only` | the support payload and every command and agent as an agentskills.io skill under `.agents/skills/` | hooks, user-only invocation, `$ARGUMENTS`, hints, tiers |\n\nThe **support payload** is the claude-code install minus what only Claude Code reads (`.claude/commands/`,\n`agents/`, `hooks/`, `output-styles/`, `skills/`, `settings.json`). The rendered commands still call\n`.claude/scripts/` and read `.claude/rules/`, so the payload ships with every target.\n\n`--dry-run` prints the plan, one `degraded:` line per `false` matrix cell and one `partial:` line per\n`partial:` cell, and writes nothing. A Claude-only command (`targets: claude-code`) is `[skipped]` on the\nother targets, and a construct a target cannot hold is `[unsupported]` by name, never paraphrased.\n\nIn a git repo whose `core.hooksPath` is unset, `arc init` points it at `.claude/templates/githooks/`\n(branch guard and staged-secret scan). It leaves a project's own hooks path alone and says so.\n\n## Read an install back\n\n```bash\nnode bin/arc.mjs doctor --dir /path/to/project     # or: node .claude/scripts/engine/arc-install.mjs --doctor DIR\nnode bin/arc.mjs doctor                            # checks this copy of arc can install at all\n```\n\nOne line per managed path, then the counts:\n\n| State | Meaning | What to do |\n|---|---|---|\n| `placed` | on disk, byte-identical (CR bytes ignored) to what the install wrote | nothing |\n| `missing` | the install wrote it, and it is gone | re-run `arc init` with the same target |\n| `unmanaged-conflict` | something else is there: a hand edit, a link, a directory | keep it, or re-run with `--force`; the original goes to `.arc-install-backup/<stamp>/` |\n| `degraded` | a matrix cell the target cannot hold | nothing: it is a declared limit |\n","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":60,"totalLines":101,"truncated":true}},"title":"docs\\runbooks\\distribute.md","time":{"start":1791874603993,"end":1791874604015}},"id":"prt_1340c9a54001jHnmg2R0LJONc4","sessionID":"ses_ecbf849dcffe1ywd0dEC0OOYDy","messageID":"msg_1340c35650012nRtOvsiF0zpox"}}
